 "build": "labyrinth",
 "note": "The Labyrinth's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md). The ground's KGROUND layers (84-host-ground.js): ground.steppe (the grazed steppe and meadow: ground.ground003), ground.mud (the trodden banks, the trails and the wallows: ground.brown_mud_02), ground.gravel (the river's bars and the causeways' shoulders), ground.sand (the pond's beach where the banks are low), rock.dome (the knobs' talus and the walls: the glaciated dome's banded gneiss). THE FLORA (src/50-70, the kit's own mammoth steppe): the four trees' barks (larch, birch, the Euphrates poplar's for the steppe poplar, willow) and cards (card.larch's green row, card.birch.dwarf's summer row for the silver birch until its own card is delivered: core/materials/PROMPTS-NEEDED.md section 44, card.aspen for the poplar, card.willow.woolly), the scrub (card.dwarfbirch, the woolly willow, card.juniper), the floor (card.grass.dry, card.stipa, card.sage for wormwood, card.sedge.fen, card.cottongrass, card.flower.bloom.highland, card.flowerspike), the wild melon's leaves (card.crop.melon; its fruit is plain colour until its rind is delivered: PROMPTS-NEEDED.md section 44), the cold rock's lichens (card.lichen, card.cladonia), moss, cushions (surface.cushion), the boulders (rock.gneiss.banded), the pit tarns' natives (card.lily.iridescent, card.reed under an iridescent material). The Hall and its stacks take the Ancients kit's pack. Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/labyrinth after any change, then python3 build.py.",
